Feature: site — what a Pages workflow publishes

  Background:
    Given a git-initialised instance "Demo" with a README linking to its skills README, and a skills directory

  @test:scripts/site.test.ts::site_—_what_a_Pages_workflow_publishes::stagesReadmeAndFiles
  Scenario: the README page is README.md (served as README.html); the files sit beside it; nothing is overwritten
    Given an output directory that already holds its own _config.yml
    When the site is staged into it
    Then there are no problems
    And the staged README.md has a Contents section linking to the skills section, and says it was generated by bootstrap-tools
    And there is no index.md, and index.html is the redirect page
    And skills/README.md is staged beside it
    And the existing _config.yml is unchanged and reported skipped

  @test:scripts/site.test.ts::site_—_what_a_Pages_workflow_publishes::noDeclarationNoSite
  Scenario: no declaration, no site
    When a site is staged from a directory that does not exist
    Then it throws

  @test:scripts/site.test.ts::site_—_what_a_Pages_workflow_publishes::stagesDocumentsAtIris
  Scenario: every JSON Schema and JSON-LD document is staged at the address it names, with a .json copy of JSON-LD
    Given an instance "vocab" at version 1.2.3 with iriBase "https://x.example/vocab/", a schema and a ns.jsonld under its v1 address, and a JSON file whose $id is on another host
    Then its published documents are the JSON-LD ns at "v1/ns" and the JSON Schema at "v1/schemas/a.schema.json", and nothing else
    And the JSON-LD document is staged at "v1/ns" and "v1/ns.json"
    When the site is staged
    Then there are no problems
    And v1/ns, v1/ns.json, v1/ns.jsonld and v1/schemas/a.schema.json all exist
    And v1/ns holds exactly the bytes of ns.jsonld
    And the README page has an anchored "Published documents" heading and a contents link to it
    And the documents section links the ns address with a .json copy

  @test:scripts/site.test.ts::site_—_what_a_Pages_workflow_publishes::landingRedirectsToReadme
  Scenario: the default landing page redirects to README.html; an instance's own index wins
    Then the redirect page refreshes to README.html and names it canonical
    Given an instance "landing" with its own index.md
    When its site is staged
    Then no index.html is written
    And index.md is the instance's own

  @test:scripts/site.test.ts::site_—_what_a_Pages_workflow_publishes::footerNamesGeneratorOrSource
  Scenario: a generated page's footer names its generator and source, never an edit page; an authored one edits its SOURCE
    Given the repository "https://github.com/o/r" on branch main
    Then a wholly generated skills/README.md's footer names scripts/subgraph-readmes.ts as generator, "the entry" as its source, and the skills tree as source URL
    And a partly generated README.md's footer is an edit URL for README.md plus scripts/readme-sections.ts as the generator of a section
    And an authored page with no repository has an empty footer

  @test:scripts/site.test.ts::site_—_what_a_Pages_workflow_publishes::layoutReplacesThemeFooter
  Scenario: the staged layout replaces the theme footer, and _config.yml scopes each page's footer
    Given an instance "footer" of repository o/r with an authored skills/a.md
    When its site is staged
    Then the default layout has no github_edit_link
    And _config.yml scopes skills/a.md with its edit URL on main
    And _config.yml scopes README.md as generated by scripts/readme-book.ts

  @test:scripts/site.test.ts::site_—_what_a_Pages_workflow_publishes::noIriBaseNoAddresses
  Scenario: no iriBase, no document addresses: nothing claimed
    Then the Demo instance, which has no iriBase, has no published documents
